BRIEF.md

# The machine's own output. Ignored so a fresh clone starts at run 1 with an
# empty trend, rather than inheriting someone else's run counter and
# rejection-rate history and reporting them as its own.
#
# A reader should still be able to see what the machine produced and what it
# stopped without running anything, so a frozen copy of one pass is committed
# under sample-run/ instead. See sample-run/README.md.
# Leading slash matters: these are anchored to the repo root so that the
# frozen copies under sample-run/ are still committed. Without it, `out/`
# matches at any depth and silently swallows sample-run/out/ as well.
/out/
/quarantine/
/logs/
/state.json
/REVIEW_QUEUE.md

# macOS finder droppings.
.DS_Store

